<title>LITHUANIA: YIELDS FALL AT SALE OF 182-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELDS FALL AT SALE OF 182-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield at an auction of</p>
<p>182-day Treasury bills fell on Tuesday and demand exceeded</p>
<p>supply, the central bank said.</p>
<p>All amounts are in millions of litas.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AV YIELD   LAST TIME   MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID  SOLD</p>
<p> 182-day     7.97	 9.55	7.80/7.97   30   88.062 30</p>
<p>The settlement date for today's auction was August 8, and</p>
<p>the bills mature on February 6.</p>
<p>The next auction is on August 11, when 30 million litas of</p>
<p>91-day paper will be offered.</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom +370 2 223 517</p>
</text>
